'''2.''' [''l. c.''] A plant-louse. [In this sense the plural ''aphides'' (af′i-dēz) is used.]—'''Woolly aphis.''' {{smaller|See ''Eriosoma.''}}

'''aphis-lion''' (ā′fis-lī″o̤n), ''n.'' A name for the larva of a lace-winged fly of the family ''Hemerobiidæ.''

'''aphis-sugar''' (ā′fis-shu̇g″är), ''n.'' Honey-dew, a secretion peculiar to insects of the genus ''Aphis,'' voided from their anal siphuncles.

'''aphlaston''' (a-flas′ton), ''n.'' [Gr. ἄφλαστον.] Same as ''aplustre.''

'''aphlogistic''' (af-lō-jis′tik), ''a.'' [< Gr. ἀφλόγιστος, not inflammable, < ἀ- priv. + φλογιστός, inflammable: see ''phlogiston.''] Flameless.—'''Aphlogistic lamp,''' {{smaller|a lamp in which a coil of platinum wire extending above the wick is kept constantly red-hot by the slow combustion of alcohol-vapor, heated first by the flame of the wick, but after this is extinguished by the incandescent wire.}}

